First, I want to thank everyone who participated (players, coders ad 
administrators); the Tournament couldn't happen without everyone's 
contributions.

With no returning admin volunteers (Matt being in France for the 
semester and Craig having a new son) and two new admins (Xin and Jeff) 
we had 6 production servers this year, though all were unfortunately in 
the United States. We logged a total of 16,880 completed games played by 
840 players.

Oddly, that's almost 300 more players than last year but fewer than half 
as many completed games.  We haven't run any stats on the database, but 
given that there were a few folks last year engaged in _massive_ 
character re-rolling I expect that much of the difference is that no one 
was doing that this year.  ;-)

The posted results are tentative, as the note on the page says, since 
one of the game servers crashed approximately 1.5 hours before the 
Tournament ended.  Due to how the syncronization timing is set up, that 
server could have up to 10 minutes of results on it which we need to get 
off and imported into the database before these results can be 
considered final.  I should be able to get that wrapped up tomorrow.

For next year I'm going to have to borrow a leaf from the motivational 
handbook used by Jick, from Kingdom of Loathing, and offer to let you 
all punch me in the stomach if I don't get the .nethackrc editor 
finished before launch.

Also for next year, in addition to the fixes we rolled during the 
Tournament, we've finished the fixes for the rest of the Grue Challenge 
bugs that we couldn't roll out without breaking saved game 
compatibility.  We've also changed the Challenge code so you can ignore 
a Challenge for the duration of a game, rather than having to either 
accept it immediately or ignore it for the remainder of the Tournament.

On a more speculative note, we will be asking aardvark to expand his 
patch so we can add the suggested Most Extinctionist trophy (exact name 
to-be-determined) for next year.  We hope he'll be up for it, 'cause if 
he's not I'm going to have to.  ;-)

Cheers,
-robin


